Local patch (session-08, found by UBSan in tests/unit/test_keystore):
  source/aes_encrypt.c line 86, tc_aes128_set_encrypt_key(): k[Nb*i]<<24,
  and line 67, macro subbyte(): sbox[...] << 24. Both shift a uint8_t
  promoted to int into the sign bit for octets >= 0x80 (undefined
  behaviour, C99 6.5.7p4). Cast to unsigned int first. The
  result is the same on every compiler tried; the behaviour was undefined.
  Upstream tinycrypt is archived, so the fix is kept here (security-report.md).
